The release pipeline is an original work of nodemode-ai: a watch over the app
repositories, one release workflow driven by a registry of the apps, draft
releases with SHA256SUMS, and the family catalogue FormPortal reads.

The workflows call third-party GitHub Actions under their own licences, run on
CI runners only and never distributed with any app: actions/checkout,
actions/setup-node, actions/setup-python, actions/setup-go, actions/setup-java,
actions/upload-artifact and actions/download-artifact (MIT),
dtolnay/rust-toolchain (MIT OR Apache-2.0), Swatinem/rust-cache (LGPL-3.0),
ilammy/msvc-dev-cmd (MIT), android-actions/setup-android (MIT),
docker/setup-qemu-action, docker/setup-buildx-action, docker/login-action and
docker/build-push-action (Apache-2.0), and rhysd/actionlint in the
self-check (MIT). scripts/catalog.py uses the Python cryptography package
(Apache-2.0 OR BSD-3-Clause), installed on a runner, to sign the catalogue.
